    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Malaysia was formed on 16 September 1963 from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#malaya">Malaya</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#singapore">Singapore</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sabah">Sabah</a> and Sarawak; Singapore left in 1965.</li><li>Its king is elected every five years from nine hereditary Malay rulers, a system unique in the world.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#malaysian-new-economic-policy">New Economic Policy</a> after the 1969 riots reshaped wealth between ethnic groups as the economy industrialised rapidly.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Malaysia's head of state, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#yang-di-pertuan-agong">Yang di-Pertuan Agong</a>, is chosen by secret ballot of the nine hereditary Malay rulers, who have largely followed a fixed rotation since 1957.</p></aside>
    </section>

